# Cargo build directories, at any depth — the root workspace and the app's.
#
# `**/target/` rather than `target*`: the latter is a prefix match on names, so
# a source file called `targeting.rs` or a directory called `targets/` would
# vanish from git without anyone noticing. The trailing slash keeps it to
# directories.
**/target/

# Node modules, at any depth. The root workspace and the app's.
# `**/node_modules/` rather than `node_modules*`: the latter is a prefix match on
# names, so a source file called `node_modules.rs` or a directory called
# `node_modules_backup/` would vanish from git without anyone noticing. The
# trailing slash keeps it to directories.
node_modules/

# Vendored proto dependencies — regenerate with `cargo xtask vendor-proto`.
# Committed copies of Google files would be linted as if they were ours.
/protobuf/.deps
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Local data + models — never committed
/data
/models
*.gguf
*.bin.zst
*.html

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
AGENT_*.md
AGENTS.md
docs/STATUS.md

# Evaluation datasets. Fetched by examples/datasets/download.sh.
/examples/datasets/*/

# Descriptor set consumed by `buffers generate`. A build artifact of `buf build`,
# reproducible from the protos, so it is rebuilt rather than committed.
/descriptors.binpb

# Generated Rust now lives in telividb-buffers and is committed, the same way
# telividb-proto commits its prost output: `cargo build` needs neither capnp nor
# flatc installed. Nothing to ignore here any more.
